title: Customize an HTML Element
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

There is no wikitext rule in TiddlyWiki core to produce an HTML `<details>` block, so this is a good showcase for custom-markup. With v1.0 there are two ways to do it: a ''marker tiddler'' (canonical) or an inline ''pragma'' (escape hatch).

!! What the output should look like

```
<details class="notop cbox cbox-primary hard-linebreaks" open>
	<summary class="margin-init">Details - Summary</summary>
	line 1
	line 2
</details>
```

The classes `notop`, `cbox`, `cbox-primary`, `hard-linebreaks` and `margin-init` come from this edition's stylesheet.

!! Option 1: marker tiddlers (canonical, vocabulary-engine)

Add two marker tiddlers tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Marker>>:

|! Field |! `DETAILS` marker |! `SUMMARY` marker |
|`open` |`DETAILS` |`SUMMARY` |
|`kind` |`word` |`word` |
|`mode` |`block` |`block` |
|`element` |`details` |`summary` |
|`classes` |`.notop.cbox.cbox-primary.hard-linebreaks` |`.margin-init` |
|`end-string` |`------` |(default end-of-line) |
|`attributes` |`{"open":""}` |(none) |

Group them into a vocabulary by tagging both with `Vocab/Html-Elements`, then add a meta tiddler `$:/vocab/html-elements` tagged <<tag $:/tags/CustomMarkup/Vocabulary>> with `marker-tag: Vocab/Html-Elements` and a `caption: Html-Elements`.

Activate the vocabulary on any tiddler that needs it:

```
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki;vocab=Default,Html-Elements
```

Use the markers like any other word marker:

```
DETAILS SUMMARY Details - Summary
---
line 1
line 2
------
```

`------` terminates the `DETAILS` block; `SUMMARY` consumes the rest of its line by default.

A worked example lives at [[Example - DETAILS word marker]].

!! Option 2: inline pragma (escape hatch)

For a one-off, the legacy `\custom` pragma still works. Add `;vocab=Default,Legacy-Glyphs` to the type field so the tick marker is active, then:

```
\custom tick="d" _element="details" _classes=".notop.cbox.cbox-primary.hard-linebreaks" _endString="------" open _mode=block
\custom tick="s" _element="summary" _classes=".margin-init"

´d ´s Details - Summary
---
line 1
line 2
------
```

The pragma form binds the configuration to the current tiddler only. The marker-tiddler form is wiki-wide once the vocabulary is active.

See [[Vocabulary Engine]] for the full marker-field schema and [[Migration to V1.0]] for the v0.x to v1.0 transition.
